-- allium: 3

-- Module: cost_mapping.
-- Scope: the pure mapping from a worker's cost and drain state to the value
-- the pod-deletion-cost annotation carries, to the string knarr writes for it,
-- and to the decision whether a new value is written: the sign convention,
-- what an absent annotation means, the drained value, the clamp, the
-- canonical int32 string and the change threshold (§4 Map, §5 drain states,
-- §6, §9.5). It replaces banding: there are no bands and no hysteresis.
-- Reading cost and accepting off the wire is worker_contract (§9.4a). The
-- patch and the removal, the neutral fallback and cleanup are reconcile and
-- lifecycle (§9.6, §9.12), the write budget is budget (§9.8), and the
-- per-Deployment override of the threshold is config (§9.1).
-- Owner: ticket 20 settled every question here with the maintainer on
-- 2026-10-10. Ticket 31 builds it.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Value Types
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The value the annotation carries, as the ReplicaSet controller ranks it:
-- an unannotated pod counts as 0 and lower is deleted first. 0 is absent,
-- -1 is drained, and 1 to 2147483647 is the worker's cost. No other value
-- exists; Sign, Absent, Drained and Clamp say how each is reached.
value Mapped {
    value: Integer
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Contracts
------------------------------------------------------------

contract CostMapping {
    map: (cost: Integer, draining: Boolean) -> Mapped
    render: (mapped: Mapped) -> String?
    due: (written: Mapped, next: Mapped, min_change_percent: Integer) -> Boolean

    @invariant Continuous
        -- There are no bands and no quantization. The annotation carries the
        -- worker's cost itself: map returns a positive cost unchanged,
        -- draining or not, up to the clamp. knarr never overrides the
        -- worker's cost and applies no floor.
    @invariant Sign
        -- Idle is 0 and busy is above 0. Lower is deleted first, so among
        -- pods of one ReplicaSet that tie on the earlier ranking steps a
        -- busy pod is deleted after every idle and unannotated pod, and a
        -- higher cost after a lower one. cost is not negative:
        -- worker_contract's ValidReading rejects a negative cost before map
        -- sees one.
    @invariant Absent
        -- An absent annotation means 0 and is the neutral value. A cost of 0
        -- that is not draining maps to 0, and 0 is spelled by removing the
        -- annotation: render returns null for it and the string "0" is
        -- never written. Removal, the neutral fallback (reconcile, ticket
        -- 21) and cleanup (lifecycle, ticket 23) are one operation: the
        -- same removal of the same annotation.
    @invariant Drained
        -- A reading whose worker_contract draining is true and whose cost is
        -- 0 maps to -1, which is deleted before every idle and unannotated
        -- pod. A draining reading with a positive cost maps to that cost, as
        -- Continuous says: draining changes nothing above 0.
    @invariant Clamp
        -- A cost above 2147483647 maps to 2147483647. Every mapped value is
        -- -1, 0 or 1 to 2147483647, and every one parses as int32.
    @invariant Canonical
        -- render returns the canonical signed decimal int32 string: the
        -- digits of the value with no plus sign, no leading zeros and no
        -- whitespace, "-1" for drained, and null for 0, which is no string
        -- at all. What reaches the pod is that string or the removal,
        -- nothing else.
    @invariant ChangeThreshold
        -- due is the only damping. The baseline is the last written value,
        -- never the last reading, so slow drift accumulates and is written
        -- once it adds up. due is false when next equals written: there is
        -- nothing to write. It is true whenever written or next is 0 or -1.
        -- When both are above 0 it is true exactly when the absolute
        -- difference between next and written, multiplied by 100, is at
        -- least min_change_percent multiplied by written, in integers with
        -- no rounding. min_change_percent is 0 to 100; 0 disables the
        -- threshold and every change is due. Its default is
        -- config.min_change_percent; a Deployment may override it, and the
        -- override key and an invalid override are config's (ticket 19).
    @invariant Pure
        -- map, render and due are functions of their arguments alone: the
        -- same arguments give the same results, and none reads state, time
        -- or the pod, or makes a request. Which pod state feeds map, the
        -- patch and the removal are reconcile's (ticket 31); whether a due
        -- write may go now is budget's (ticket 24).
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    min_change_percent: Integer = 10
}
